   "part": 1,
   "pin": null,
   "question": "Whether the worst case temporary duplication occurs when a sparse level L-1 causes all files to compact dense level L in one go",
   "quote": "My understanding of the worst case here is that this happens when all the data is on a single level L, with a very sparse (<32MiB) level L-1 above it. Because L-1 is so sparse, all L-1 files (with keys across the entire L level) get compacted in one go, causing the entire dense level L (~the entire database) to be temporarily copied, correct?",
   "request": "",
   "status": "open",
   "status_by": null,
   "status_note": "",
   "type": "question",
   "url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/pull/36586#discussion_r4339626383"
  },
